# CSS Notes — Recall: My Study Decks

## 1. Overview

I used CSS to make Recall look clean, simple, and comfortable to use. Since it is a study app, I wanted the layout to be easy to understand and the flashcards to be the main focus.

The design uses a blue theme with light backgrounds, rounded corners, and consistent spacing.

## 2. CSS Structure

The main stylesheet is located at `css/style.css`.

I organised the CSS into sections so that styles are easier to find and update. These sections cover:

- Base styles and typography
- Theme colours and CSS variables
- Header and navigation
- Deck cards and flashcards
- Forms and buttons
- Study progress and statistics
- Responsive layouts
- Accessibility and reduced-motion preferences

## 3. Colours and Design Choices

I used CSS custom properties for common colours and other design values. This makes it easier to keep the design consistent and update the theme without changing every selector.

The blue theme is used for important buttons and interactive elements. Light backgrounds help keep text readable, while spacing and rounded corners make the cards easier to distinguish.

## 4. Layout and Responsiveness

I used Flexbox and CSS Grid where appropriate to arrange the content.

The layout is designed to adapt to different screen sizes. On smaller screens, content can stack vertically so that deck cards, forms, and navigation remain easier to use.

I also used flexible sizing where suitable to avoid relying on fixed widths for the entire page.

## 5. Flashcard Design and Animation

Flashcards are styled to make the question and answer easy to read during study sessions.

Where card-flip animation is used, it helps create a more interactive study experience. Motion should not be necessary to understand the content, so reduced-motion preferences should also be considered.

## 6. Accessibility

I aimed to keep the interface readable and usable by:

- Maintaining clear text and background contrast.
- Keeping interactive elements visually identifiable.
- Using visible focus styles for keyboard navigation.
- Supporting smaller screens.
- Respecting the user's reduced-motion preference where animations are used.

## 7. Maintainability

I kept related styles together and used reusable classes and CSS variables wherever possible. This makes future changes easier and helps avoid repeating the same styles unnecessarily.

When updating the theme, I check for duplicate or outdated rules so that the stylesheet stays organised.

## 8. Testing

I checked the interface in the browser while building the project. I also tested the layout after making CSS changes to catch spacing, alignment, and styling issues.


